<p>4.<strong>Do-Not-Track Requests; Third-Party Tracking. </strong><span style="font-weight: 400;">We are required to track the specific location of users/devices accessing the location-restricted Services we offer. We cannot opt you out from this tracking.&nbsp; If you are casually browsing our website for information as a guest, unless your browser settings are configured to make your online activities and publicly available information about your online activities (such as Use Data described above) invisible to usage analytics tools, we do not presently have the capability to omit you from usage analytics to the extent your browser sends us a &ldquo;do not track&rdquo; message.&nbsp; However, third parties, other than our vendors or affiliates&nbsp; assisting with making the Services available do not have authorization from us to track your uses or track what other activities you may have engaged in before or after using our Services (for example, using a different website). That said, we cannot control third-party tracking and there may be some third-party tracking that occurs without our knowledge or consent.</span></p>
